      "side": 1,
      "message": "All this sounds like a good usage of memcache. Similar case needed to be solved with page tables for guest MMU stage-2 and it was done via memcache, see: https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/kernel/common/+/3702536 (and patches in this series)\n\nAlso ARM uses memcaches for that purpose both for MMU and SMMU and it is partially upstreamed: https://lists.infradead.org/pipermail/linux-arm-kernel/2022-June/756414.html.\n\nI didn\u0027t fully analyze SMMU usage but you could probably took a look how they use memcache (https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/kernel/common/+/android16-6.12:arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c?q\u003d%20kvm_hyp_memcache%20\u0026ss\u003dh%2Fandroid%2Fkernel%2Fcommon%2F%2B%2Frefs%2Fheads%2Fandroid16-6.12) - i briefly look on it and they also introduced hyp allocator for IOMMU (https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/kernel/common/+/3344128)\n\nI didn\u0027t go through all the patches so I am not telling that we have to switch to memcache right away but it sounds from this point that we probably could (and not introduce new mechanism for that)?",
